  "definition": "Disease management is a broad way of coordinating the full process of care for a disease. It often emphasizes prevention, patient counselling and education, and outpatient care instead of more costly hospital and acute care, while considering how suitable or unsuitable treatment affects both outcomes and overall cost.",
